---
import { u } from '../lib/url';

const restitutionArtists = [
  {
    name: 'Chidi Nwaubani (Looty)',
    location: 'Nigeria, UK',
    image: '/uploads/projects/01-Chidi.jpeg',
  },
  {
    name: 'Nuits Balnéaires (photography)',
    location: "Côte d'Ivoire",
    image: '/uploads/projects/02-Portrait-Nuits-Baln-C3-A9aires--Octobre-2023-_edited.jpg',
  },
  {
    name: 'Chelsea Odufu (Black Lady Goddess)',
    location: 'Nigeria, Guiana, United States',
    image: '/uploads/projects/03-DSC00595_edited-20-1-.webp',
  },
  {
    name: 'Ibaaku (Musical performance)',
    location: 'Senegal',
    image: '/uploads/projects/04-IBAAKU-9_edited.jpg',
  },
];

const heritageArtists = [
  {
    name: "Nuits Balnéaires (Côte-D'Ivoire)",
    role: 'Photographer, visual artist and poet,',
    work: "presents: l'amour est ce qu'il reste quand on aura tout oublié.",
    image: '/uploads/projects/05-7273cd_3c5c0dc0b45b4dff988168492474d604-mv2.jpg',
  },
  {
    name: 'Tobi Onabolu (Nigeria, UK)',
    role: 'Artist-Filmmaker and writer,',
    work: 'presents: The Constant is Flux.',
    image: '/uploads/projects/06-Bildschirmfoto-202025-10-16-20um-2000_19_edite.jpg',
  },
];
---

<article class="projects-page">
  <section class="project-section project-section--first" aria-labelledby="restitution-title">
    <header class="project-header">
      <h1 id="restitution-title">Restitution...et après?</h1>
      <p class="project-subtitle">an itinerary project</p>
      <div class="project-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </header>

    <div class="project-grid project-grid--restitution">
      <div class="project-copy">
        <p>
          “African cultural heritage needs to be restituted.” This claim,
          widely voiced by African cultural and political actors since the
          independence era, has gained renewed visibility in recent years.
        </p>
        <p>
          Yet, beyond its apparent urgency, restitution remains a complex and
          multifaceted process that raises critical questions: What should be
          restituted, and to whom? Under what conditions? Can restitution ever
          be complete? And more importantly, what happens after return?
        </p>
        <p>
          <em>Restitution… and then what?</em> is an itinerant curatorial and
          research-based project initiated in 2024 that seeks to move beyond the
          moment of restitution itself, in order to examine its long-term
          cultural, social, and artistic implications across African and
          diasporic contexts.
        </p>
        <p>
          Combining exhibitions, public programs, and editorial formats, the
          project creates a space for dialogue between artists, researchers, and
          cultural practitioners, exploring how restitution contributes to the
          (re)construction of cultural identity, the reactivation of collective
          memory, and the transmission and reinterpretation of cultural
          heritage.
        </p>
        <p>
          Informed by ongoing research, including a Master’s thesis focusing on
          Benin as a case study following the restitution of 26 royal artifacts,
          the project adopts a transnational and forward-looking perspective,
          engaging with both material and immaterial dimensions of heritage and
          restitution.
        </p>
        <p>
          By fostering critical reflection and exchange, it aims to address a
          key gap in current debates by shifting the focus from restitution as
          an event to restitution as an ongoing process shaping cultural
          futures, with particular attention to questions of heritage,
          sovereignty, transmission, and sustainable cultural development.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="project-artists" aria-label="Restitution artists">
        <p class="artist-intro">
          Meet the first 4 artists of this project<br />
          and their respective projects presented 23.05-06.06.2024<br />
          at Institut français Mainz.
        </p>

        <div class="artist-grid artist-grid--four">
          {restitutionArtists.map((artist) => (
            <figure>
              <img src={u(artist.image)} alt={artist.name} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <figcaption>
                <strong>{artist.name}</strong>
                <span>{artist.location}</span>
              </figcaption>
            </figure>
          ))}
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <p class="project-cta">
      <a class="catalogue-link" href={u('/uploads/catalogues/restitution-et-apres-catalogue.pdf')} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        View Catalogue
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="section-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <section class="project-section project-section--heritage" aria-labelledby="heritage-title">
    <header class="project-header project-header--compact">
      <h2 id="heritage-title">Héritage...<br />Mémoires en mouvement?</h2>
      <p class="project-date">05.December 2025 - 30.January 2026</p>
      <div class="project-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    </header>

    <div class="project-grid project-grid--heritage">
      <div class="project-copy">
        <p>
          Everything is movement. Humanity itself is movement- the very core of
          our existence. As Achille Mbembe reminds us, the history of humanity
          is a history of circulation.
        </p>
        <p>
          But if everything moves, what remains of us?<br />
          In Cotonou-the project’s first stop outside Europe, Nuits Balnéaires
          and Tobi Onabolu engage with themes of identity, heritage, memory, and
          transformation. Through their works: <em>Love Is What Remains When We
          Have Forgotten Everything</em> and <em>The Constant Is Flux</em>, they
          open a dialogue between material and immaterial archives, expanding
          the limits of collective memory and awakening echoes of the past
          within us.
        </p>
        <p>
          Who are we when everything is in motion?<br />
          What endures of the body, of being, of memory?<br />
          What remains when things relocate, transform, or fade?
        </p>
        <p class="small-copy">
          The exhibition in Benin was curated by Cheria Essieke-Bayer with the
          New Afro team in collaboration with Gallery Zato (Benin), with the
          support of Institut français Bénin, Ambassade de France au Bénin,
          Institut Goethe-Togo, die Deutsche Botschaft in Benin, Mansa,
          OffResort and Schloss Vaux.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="heritage-artists" aria-label="Héritage artists">
        {heritageArtists.map((artist) => (
          <figure>
            <figcaption>
              <strong>{artist.name} :</strong>
              <span>{artist.role}</span>
              <em>{artist.work}</em>
            </figcaption>
            <img src={u(artist.image)} alt={artist.name} loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </figure>
        ))}
      </aside>
    </div>

    <p class="project-cta">
      <a class="catalogue-link" href={u('/uploads/catalogues/heritage-memoires-en-mouvement-catalogue.pdf')} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        View Catalogue
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</article>

<style>
  .projects-page {
    min-height: 100vh;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 50% 12%, rgba(125, 76, 20, 0.9), transparent 38%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, #4c2b08 0%, #3a1d04 48%, #4c2b08 100%);
    color: #fff9eb;
    padding: clamp(36px, 5vw, 72px) 24px clamp(72px, 8vw, 112px);
  }

  .project-section {
    width: min(980px, 100%);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .project-section--first {
    padding-top: clamp(10px, 2vw, 26px);
  }

  .project-header {
    width: min(1120px, 100%);
    text-align: center;
    margin: 0 auto clamp(66px, 8vw, 112px);
  }

  .project-header h1,
  .project-header h2 {
    font-family: var(--na-font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 0.95;
    color: #fff9eb;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .project-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(70px, 8.2vw, 118px);
  }

  .project-header h2 {
    font-size: clamp(48px, 7vw, 90px);
  }

  .project-subtitle {
    font-family: var(--na-font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.8vw, 46px);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 14px auto 34px;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .project-date {
    margin: 18px auto 42px;
    font-family: var(--na-font-body);
    font-size: clamp(14px, 1.5vw, 18px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .project-rule {
    width: 290px;
    max-width: 60vw;
    height: 1px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    background: rgba(255, 249, 235, 0.6);
  }

  .project-grid {
    display: grid;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .project-grid--restitution {
    grid-template-columns: 0.88fr 1.12fr;
    gap: clamp(42px, 6vw, 76px);
  }

  .project-grid--heritage {
    grid-template-columns: 0.9fr 1.1fr;
    gap: clamp(48px, 6vw, 78px);
  }

  .project-copy {
    font-family: var(--na-font-body);
    font-size: clamp(14px, 1.15vw, 16px);
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-align: justify;
  }

  .project-copy p {
    margin: 0 0 22px;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .project-copy em {
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .small-copy {
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .artist-intro {
    font-family: var(--na-font-body);
    font-size: clamp(13px, 1vw, 15px);
    line-height: 1.35;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-align: center;
    margin: 0 auto 24px;
    max-width: 42ch;
  }

  .artist-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 76px 34px;
  }

  .artist-grid--four {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .artist-grid figure,
  .heritage-artists figure {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .artist-grid img,
  .heritage-artists img {
    width: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    background: #fff9eb;
    border: 6px solid #fff9eb;
    display: block;
  }

  .artist-grid img {
    aspect-ratio: 3 / 4;
  }

  .artist-grid figcaption {
    padding-top: 12px;
    font-family: var(--na-font-body);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.25;
    color: #fff9eb;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .artist-grid strong,
  .artist-grid span,
  .heritage-artists strong,
  .heritage-artists span,
  .heritage-artists em {
    display: block;
  }

  .project-cta {
    margin: clamp(54px, 7vw, 78px) auto 0;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .catalogue-link {
    min-width: 232px;
    min-height: 44px;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 9px 44px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: #fff9eb;
    color: #4a2b08;
    font-family: var(--na-font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 20px;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .catalogue-link:hover {
    color: #4a2b08;
    background: #ded9c7;
  }

  .section-divider {
    width: min(680px, calc(100% - 48px));
    height: 1px;
    margin: clamp(54px, 7vw, 82px) auto clamp(50px, 7vw, 78px);
    background: rgba(255, 249, 235, 0.5);
  }

  .project-header--compact {
    margin-bottom: clamp(58px, 7vw, 88px);
  }

  .heritage-artists {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(22px, 3vw, 34px);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .heritage-artists figure:first-child {
    padding-top: clamp(86px, 10vw, 132px);
  }

  .heritage-artists figcaption {
    min-height: 120px;
    margin-bottom: 22px;
    font-family: var(--na-font-body);
    font-size: clamp(13px, 1.2vw, 17px);
    line-height: 1.25;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #fff9eb;
  }

  .heritage-artists em {
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .heritage-artists img {
    aspect-ratio: 0.84;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .project-grid,
    .project-grid--restitution,
    .project-grid--heritage {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .project-header {
      margin-bottom: 48px;
    }

    .project-copy {
      text-align: left;
    }

    .heritage-artists figure:first-child {
      padding-top: 0;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .projects-page {
      padding-inline: 20px;
    }

    .project-header h1 {
      font-size: clamp(54px, 18vw, 86px);
    }

    .project-header h2 {
      font-size: clamp(42px, 15vw, 72px);
    }

    .artist-grid--four,
    .heritage-artists {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 36px;
    }

    .heritage-artists figcaption {
      min-height: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
